      "content": "it's just hard to see how anything else makes sense when you put it that way. like if even the act of \"clinging\" is just a form of delusion, then maybe the only way to actually be authentic to the universe is to stop fighting it. if the most honest thing we can do is acknowledge the void, does that mean there's a certain kind of peace or dignity in just letting go of the struggle entirely?",
